- label: goal judge treats the plan as a HYPOTHESIS not a spec: PASS means matches the GOAL never the plan; plan-asserted concrete values not quoted from goal/test files are re-derived, contradictions NACK citing both values (plan-asserted=X vs goal-derived=Y); [DERIVED] decisions are spot-checked, [ASSUMED] re-derived; judge and blind recheck verify single-answer deliverables by a method different in kind and state it
  command: grep -qF 'HYPOTHESIS, not a spec' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'plan-asserted=X vs goal-derived=Y' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF '[ASSUMED] decisions MUST be re-derived' tools/goal.mjs && test "$(grep -c 'different IN KIND' tools/goal.mjs)" -ge 2 && grep -qF 'state which method you used' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
# project

- label: all tests pass
  command: npm test

# package
- label: package name is
  command: grep -q '"name": "@avcodes/mi"' package.json
  tags: [avcodes/mi]
- label: ESM module (type: module in package.json)
  command: grep -q '"type": "module"' package.json
- label: bin entry maps 'mi' to ./index.mjs
  command: node -e "const p=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('package.json'));process.exit(p.bin?.mi==='./index.mjs'?0:1)"
- label: zero npm dependencies — Node builtins and native fetch only
  command: node -e "const p=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('package.json'));process.exit(p.dependencies?1:0)"
- label: published files are index.mjs, tools/, and skills/ only
  command: node -e "const p=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('package.json'));const f=p.files;process.exit(f.length===3&&f.includes('index.mjs')&&f.includes('tools')&&f.includes('skills')?0:1)"
- label: MIT license
  command: grep -q '"license": "MIT"' package.json

# architecture
- core logic lives in index.mjs — every non-shebang line is intentionally dense
- label: tools hot-load from tools/*.mjs via dynamic import before each model call
  command: grep -q 'await loadTools(); const response' index.mjs
- label: tools loaded from two search paths: bundled (MI_DIR/tools/) then user (MI_HOME/tools/); user tools override by name
  command: grep -q 'MI_HOME.*tools' index.mjs
- tool modules default-export { name, description, parameters, handler }
- label: skills are markdown playbooks in skills/<name>/SKILL.md with YAML frontmatter
  command: test -f skills/debug/SKILL.md && head -1 skills/debug/SKILL.md | grep -q '^---'
- skills loaded from two search paths: bundled (MI_DIR/skills/) then user (~/.agents/skills/)
- label: no build step, no transpilation, no lint config
  command: ! test -f tsconfig.json && ! test -f .eslintrc.json && ! test -f webpack.config.js
- Node builtins exposed globally for tool modules: spawn, readFileSync, existsSync, readdirSync, homedir

# tools
- label: bundled tools include bash, delegate, goal, and skill
  command: test $(ls tools/*.mjs | wc -l) -eq 4 && test -f tools/bash.mjs && test -f tools/delegate.mjs && test -f tools/goal.mjs && test -f tools/skill.mjs
- label: bash tool runs commands in detached process groups for clean signal handling
  command: grep -q 'detached.*true' tools/bash.mjs
- label: bash tool supports timeout (ms) and background (bg) modes
  command: grep -q 'timeout' tools/bash.mjs && grep -q 'bg' tools/bash.mjs
- label: bash tool recovers provider-emitted nested arguments JSON payloads
  command: grep -q 'args.arguments' tools/bash.mjs && grep -q 'JSON.parse(args.arguments)' tools/bash.mjs
- label: background bash writes output to /tmp/mi-{timestamp}.log, returns pid and log path
  command: grep -q '/tmp/mi-' tools/bash.mjs
- label: background bash records per-mi-process managed jobs
  command: grep -q 'MI_SESSION_ID' tools/bash.mjs && grep -q '/tmp/mi-jobs-' tools/bash.mjs && grep -q 'jobs=truthy lists background jobs' tools/bash.mjs
- label: goal loop establishes refined exit criteria before worker iterations
  command: grep -q 'you are the planner for a goal loop' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'EXIT_CRITERIA' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'VERIFIER_SHAPE_CONTRACT' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'VERIFICATION_PLAN' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'Refined Exit Criteria And Verification Plan' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal planner synthesizes verifier shape contract from visible task evidence
  command: grep -q 'infer verifier shape' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'exact artifact paths' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'numeric thresholds' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'preservation constraints' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal worker iterations receive refined exit criteria and prior feedback, not raw judge criteria
  command: grep -q 'verifier contract and plan' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'judge feedback and checkpoint' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'one noninteractive bash script' tools/goal.mjs && ! grep -q 'judge criteria: ${check}' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal loop appends structured iteration summaries to its progress log
  command: grep -q 'Iteration ${i} Summary' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'worker summary:' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'judge summary:' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'worker tail:' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'judge tail:' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal loop writes markdown and JSONL progress logs with iteration events
  command: grep -q "events = log.replace" tools/goal.mjs && grep -q "emit('start'" tools/goal.mjs && grep -q "emit('iteration'" tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'event log:' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal judges must not invent criteria beyond the goal and check
  command: grep -q 'do not invent criteria' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'NEVER trust worker-reported values' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'skipped, approximate, or uncertain' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal judges must measure thresholds and exact artifact contracts before ACK
  command: grep -q 'EXACT stated threshold' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'measured=X expected=Y' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'exact path exists' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal tool supports deadline parameter for budget-aware iteration with 4-phase guidance and salvage policy
  command: grep -q 'deadline.*unix timestamp' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'budgetPhase' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'SALVAGE' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'FINAL SALVAGE' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal judge uses strict 8-rule verification protocol — exact thresholds with 5%-margin risk note, adversarial edge-case checks
  command: grep -q 'STRICT VERIFICATION' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'within 5% of the bar as a risk' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'adversarial checks' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal worker receives strategy diversity enforcement with failed strategy fingerprints
  command: grep -q 'strategies.push' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'failed strategies (do NOT repeat)' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'abandon this solution family entirely' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal worker receives structured checkpoints for iteration handoff instead of raw judge output
  command: grep -q 'STRATEGY:' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'FILES_MODIFIED' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'COMMANDS_SUCCEEDED' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'BLOCKERS' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'checkpoint' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal strategy history is capped at last 5 entries to prevent prompt bloat
  command: grep -q 'slice(-5)' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal planner runs explicit inspection checklist before reasoning (directory listing, project structure, output file check)
  command: grep -q 'run at most 12 commands' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'pwd && ls -la' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'check if output files from the goal already exist' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal worker prompt includes bash discipline guidance (command timeouts, output piping, noninteractive scripts)
  command: grep -q 'timeout commands >60s' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'pipe verbose output through tail -50' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'one noninteractive bash script' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal worker gets budget-derived timeout (remaining - 120s) when deadline is set
  command: grep -q 'iterTimeout.*deadline.*budget.*120' tools/goal.mjs
- skill tool without name lists all available skills; with name returns SKILL.md body
- label: skill frontmatter parsed via regex (^name: and ^description: with multiline flag)
  command: grep -q '/m' tools/skill.mjs
- label: goal ACK triggers blind skeptical recheck (idle-budget gated) that sees only the task, not the plan, and enumerates every requirement element
  command: grep -q 'BLIND SKEPTICAL RECHECK' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'no worker plan, no worker claims' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'enumerate EVERY requirement element' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'i <= 2 || (budget() ?? 0) > 300' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'CONCRETE measured-vs-required mismatch' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal judge and recheck probes are observational only — never write to service control channels (monitor sockets, FIFOs, admin endpoints)
  command: test $(grep -c 'NEVER write to service control channels' tools/goal.mjs) -eq 2 && grep -q 'monitor sockets, FIFOs' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal judge and blind recheck are strictly read-only — no file writes, git write ops, or installs; mismatches route to the worker via NACK
  command: test $(grep -c 'STRICTLY READ-ONLY' tools/goal.mjs) -eq 2 && grep -q 'commit/merge/cherry-pick/rebase/checkout/reset/branch/clean/stash/apply' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'so the WORKER performs the repair' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal worker restart-before-ACK guidance carves out VMs/emulators/long-boot systems — never restart those
  command: grep -q 'VM/emulator/long-boot system — never restart those' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal planner emits ARTIFACTS: line; draft gate prefixes worker with draft-first directive when artifacts missing past 15% budget, without producing NACKs or feeding blockerSigs
  command: grep -q 'ARTIFACTS:' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'draftGate' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF '> 0.15' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'DRAFT FIRST' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q "emit('draft_gate'" tools/goal.mjs
- label: MI_JUDGE_MODEL and MI_JUDGE_PARAMS optionally override model/params for judge and skeptical recheck delegates only
  command: grep -q 'MI_JUDGE_MODEL' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'MI_JUDGE_PARAMS' tools/goal.mjs && test $(grep -c 'env: jenv' tools/goal.mjs) -eq 2
- label: goal loop shares one bg-jobs registry per session (MI_SESSION_ID) and polls live jobs without LLM calls — MI_JOB_POLL_MS interval, stall guard, cumulative 50%-of-budget cap
  command: grep -q 'MI_SESSION_ID' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'MI_JOB_POLL_MS' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'monTotalMs' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'liveJobs' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'stalls < 3' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal planner emits INVARIANTS section (input-derived conservation checks) and judge rule 6b executes them against pristine input before ACK
  command: grep -q 'INVARIANTS' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q '6b\.' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'PRISTINE input' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'self-referential' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal verdict quarantine: verdicts need an ACK/NACK token plus evidence (measured=/PASS/FAIL); garbled judge output gets exactly one retry then counts as NACK; garbled recheck output keeps the primary ACK (recheck_invalid event)
  command: grep -q 'judge_invalid' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'recheck_invalid' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'measured=|PASS|FAIL' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal verdict scans the full judge message and takes the last ACK/NACK-bearing line — a front-loaded ACK with long trailing rationale parses as ACK
  command: grep -q 'findLast' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal judge and skeptical recheck delegates get a wall-clamped timeout (45-180s scaled from budget); recheck is skipped entirely when budget < 180s, banking the ACK
  command: grep -q 'wallT' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'recheck_skipped' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal salvage/urgent phases trigger adaptively from an EMA of iteration duration (SALVAGE at max(60, 1.3*EMA); URGENT at max(2.5*EMA, 20% total)), EMA contribution clamped to 25% of total budget
  command: grep -q '1.3 \* e' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q '2.5 \* e' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal per-iteration verification-cost cap — iteration 1 gets 1/3 of usable budget, later EXPLORE iterations the full remaining, but COMMIT/URGENT iterations are bounded to 50% of remaining (matching the judge wallT cap) so a runaway refine/verify sweep on a working-enough artifact is cut off with budget left for SALVAGE
  command: grep -qF 'iterFrac = i === 1 ? 0.333 : phase === ' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF "* 1000 * iterFrac" tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal draft-gate escalates one-shot past 40% elapsed budget with no live jobs: worker prompt becomes an artifacts-first salvage-style directive whose NACK is exempt from strategy/blockerSig accounting
  command: grep -q 'ARTIFACT ESCALATION' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'escalated' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF '> 0.4' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal judge executes script deliverables with the plainest task-implied interpreter (python file.py, not venv/alias) before ACK — crash/import error is NACK; skips execution only when running would mutate state, stating why
  command: grep -q 'PLAINEST interpreter invocation' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal judge NACKs un-re-derivable single-value answers unless the worker log shows a second independent derivation method agreeing (cross-validation demand)
  command: grep -q 'second independent method and show both agree' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal judge re-derives any spec-recipe quantity (defined via an explicit recipe/region/subset/window/formula) strictly from the goal's LITERAL scope not the worker's chosen basis, treats that named scope as a CONSTRAINT measured against the goal's stated bound, and NACKs a worker-basis vs goal-literal-basis divergence naming it
  command: grep -qF 'MEASUREMENT-BASIS:' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF "goal's LITERAL scope" tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'worker-basis=' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal judge runs a final-state sweep before ACK: every goal-stated end-state property is re-measured NOW, goal-quoted literals compared byte-for-byte, never against memory of an earlier check
  command: grep -q 'FINAL-STATE SWEEP' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal planner emits a CONSTRAINTS section quoting every goal-stated bound/enumerated item/format rule verbatim as CONSTRAINT lines; judge must emit a MEASURED line per CONSTRAINT or NACK
  command: grep -qF 'prefixed "CONSTRAINT:"' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'EVERY "CONSTRAINT:" line in the plan' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal judge and salvage carry a mechanical kill-verb ban (kill/pkill/killall/kill %/QEMU quit/system_powerdown); salvage output mentioning kill verbs emits a salvage_kill_violation event
  command: grep -qF 'banned: kill, pkill, killall' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'MECHANICAL BAN' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF "emit('salvage_kill_violation'" tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal judge runs a grader-perspective probe — named module/script/CLI deliverables must import/execute under the goal-stated name from a neutral cwd; placement/import failure is NACK even if in-place checks pass
  command: grep -qF 'grader-perspective probe' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'NEUTRAL cwd' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal pivot mandate arms on 2 consecutive identical judge-NACK signatures regardless of artifacts — repairing in place with the same method is banned for that iteration and a pivot_armed event is emitted
  command: grep -qF 'pivotArmed' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF "emit('pivot_armed'" tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'blockerSigs.slice(-2)' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal judge runs an external-client runtime probe for service/API tasks — every goal-documented endpoint/RPC exercised with a fresh curl/grpcurl/client call asserting goal-stated status/response; worker transcript claims are never evidence; destructive endpoints probed only on disposable fixtures or verified statically
  command: grep -qF 'external-client runtime probe' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'FRESH external client' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'disposable fixture data' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal planner, worker, and judge enforce a verbatim-identifier guard — goal-named identifiers (fields, endpoints, files, flags, message/service names) are used character-for-character, unstated names default to the conventional/spec-standard choice recorded as an AMBIGUITIES DECISION, and the judge audits declared identifiers byte-for-byte against the goal text
  command: test $(grep -c 'character-for-character' tools/goal.mjs) -ge 2 && grep -qF 'identifier naming is a fork class' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'identifier audit' tools/goal.mjs && test $(grep -c 'value not val' tools/goal.mjs) -ge 2
  tags: [implemented]

# agent-loop
- agent loop streams OpenAI chat completions via SSE, executes tool calls, repeats until text response
- SSE parser buffers incomplete frames, splits on double-newline, skips [DONE] and malformed JSON
- tool call fragments streamed by index — id/type overwrite, name/arguments append
- label: tool output logged truncated to 200 chars; full result sent to model
  command: grep -q '200' index.mjs
- unknown tool calls return error listing available tools instead of crashing

# cli
- four CLI modes: interactive REPL, one-shot (-p), stdin pipe, and goal loop (-g)
- /reset command splices history to keep only system prompt
- REPL error recovery pops failed user message so model never sees it
- version banner prints '◰ mi/<version>' in orange and gray ANSI
- label: ANSI color helpers: gray (90), red (31), orange (38;5;208)
  command: grep -q '208' index.mjs

# system-prompt
- system prompt = SYSTEM_PROMPT env (full override) or built-in DEFAULT_PROMPT
- label: default prompt enforces terse raw-terminal transcript persona
  command: grep -q 'quiet, mechanical, precise' index.mjs && grep -q 'at most one status line under 8 words' index.mjs
- system message appends: CWD, ISO date, -f file content, AGENTS.md (if present), skill summaries
- label: AGENTS.md auto-ingested from CWD and appended to system prompt
  command: grep -q 'AGENTS.md' index.mjs

# env
- label: default model is gpt-5.4 (MODEL env var)
  command: grep -q 'gpt-5.4' index.mjs
- label: default API base is https://api.openai.com (OPENAI_BASE_URL env var)
  command: grep -q 'api.openai.com' index.mjs
- OPENAI_API_KEY required for all modes except help/version (-h, --help, -v, --version)
- label: REASONING_EFFORT is optional and omitted from API requests when unset
  command: grep -q 'reasoning_effort.*REASONING_EFFORT' index.mjs
- label: MI_API_PARAMS is optional JSON merged into chat completion payload
  command: grep -q 'MI_API_PARAMS.*JSON.parse' index.mjs
- MI_DIR and MI_PATH set in process.env for tools/skills to locate package assets
- label: OPENAI_BASE_URL accepts provider roots with or without trailing /v1
  command: grep -q 'api = p =>' index.mjs
- label: CLI supports -d flag and MI_DEADLINE env var for goal deadline
  command: grep -q "getArg('-d')" index.mjs && grep -q 'MI_DEADLINE' index.mjs && grep -q 'deadline: +dl' index.mjs

# skills
- label: 11 bundled skills: debug, delegate, explore, new-skill, plan, refactor, review, self, tasks, tdd, verify
  command: test $(ls -d skills/*/SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l) -eq 11
- label: user skills live in ~/.agents/skills/ and are merged with bundled skills
  command: test -d skills/debug

# testing
- label: test suite uses node --test with mocked OpenAI-compatible HTTP server
  command: grep -q 'node --test' package.json
- tests cover: CLI modes, SSE streaming, tool calls, tool hot-loading, REPL reset, error recovery, SIGINT, AGENTS.md, skills, Unicode
- label: npm run lines counts meaningful LOC in index.mjs only — target is 30
  command: grep -q 'count-lines' package.json
- label: count-lines.mjs is language-aware: strips comments and blank lines for JS, Python, and Shell
  command: test -f scripts/count-lines.mjs
- label: auxiliary tests: test_exit.js (exit codes) and test_sigint.cjs (signal handling) — not in npm test
  command: test -f tests/test_exit.js && test -f tests/test_sigint.cjs

# publishing
- label: publishing triggered by GitHub Release or workflow_dispatch
  command: test -f .github/workflows/publish.yml
- label: uses OIDC tokenless publish with provenance — no NPM_TOKEN secret
  command: grep -q 'provenance' .github/workflows/publish.yml
- label: CI requires Node 24.x
  command: grep -q '24' .github/workflows/publish.yml

# harbor
- label: bench/ holds the Harbor installed agent for mi (bench.mi_agent:MiAgent), job configs, a pinned Harbor wrapper and compare.py; evaluation-only, excluded from the npm package
  command: test -f bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'class MiAgent(BaseInstalledAgent)' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q '^bench/' .npmignore
- label: benchmark scenarios are Harbor JobConfigs stacked on bench/configs/mi.yaml and run through npm scripts (bench:smoke, bench:subset, bench:full) with Harbor pinned to 0.23.0
  command: test -f bench/configs/smoke.yaml && test -f bench/configs/subset.yaml && test -f bench/configs/full.yaml && grep -q 'bench/configs/mi.yaml -c bench/configs/subset.yaml' package.json && grep -q 'harbor==${HARBOR_VERSION:-0.23.0}' bench/harbor.sh
- label: tasks are pulled from the Harbor registry (terminal-bench/terminal-bench-2-1), never vendored
  command: grep -q 'name: terminal-bench/terminal-bench-2-1' bench/configs/full.yaml && ! test -d bench/terminal-bench-2.1
- label: harbor adapter uploads the local checkout to /opt/mi and runs mi in goal mode with TERMINAL_BENCH_CHECK and the eval system prompt
  command: grep -q 'upload_dir(self._staged_checkout(), "/opt/mi")' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q -- '-g "$1" -c "$MI_GOAL_CHECK"' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'EVAL_SYSTEM_PROMPT' bench/mi_agent.py
- label: harbor adapter recomputes the trial's agent timeout from config.json + task.toml and sets MI_TASK_TIMEOUT, MI_DEADLINE (60s verifier buffer) and MI_GOAL_MAX (4-12)
  command: grep -q 'TrialConfig.model_validate_json' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'MI_TASK_TIMEOUT - 60' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'MI_GOAL_MAX' tools/goal.mjs
- label: harbor TERMINAL_BENCH_CHECK treats /tests/ results as ground truth for what they cover, requires every goal-stated path/threshold with measured values, never NACKs for margin, and warns about the hidden external verifier
  command: grep -q 'test results are GROUND TRUTH' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'hidden external verifier' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'EVERY goal-stated output path' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'never NACK for margin' bench/mi_agent.py
- label: harbor adapter writes an AGENTS.md workspace snapshot in the detected workdir before the goal loop
  command: grep -q 'Workspace Snapshot' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'detect_workdir' bench/mi_agent.py
- label: eval determinism knobs are agent kwargs (temperature 0, seed 42, OpenRouter provider pin alibaba with allow_fallbacks false) merged into MI_API_PARAMS; the pin applies only to openrouter models
  command: grep -Pzq 'temperature: 0\n\s+seed: 42\n\s+provider: alibaba' bench/configs/mi.yaml && grep -q '"allow_fallbacks": False' bench/mi_agent.py && grep -q 'provider == "openrouter"' bench/mi_agent.py
- label: bench/compare.py reads Harbor job/trial result.json (Harbor's mean and pass@k shown as-is), pools trials per task, and gives per-task Fisher exact plus a smoothed z-test SIGNAL/NOISE verdict on common tasks
  command: python3 -c "import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'bench'); import compare as c; assert abs(c.fisher_exact_two_sided(3,0,0,3)-0.1)<1e-9; assert abs(c.fisher_exact_two_sided(5,0,0,5)-2/252)<1e-9"
- label: past benchmark scores and findings live in docs/benchmark-history.md; old run data is archived at ~/archive/mi-bench-2026-09-26/
  command: grep -q '38/89' docs/benchmark-history.md && grep -q '50/89' docs/benchmark-history.md && grep -q 'mi-bench-2026-09-26' docs/benchmark-history.md

# benchmark
- label: goal loop skips LLM judge with a mechanical NACK while no declared artifact exists — mech NACKs are exempt from strategy/blockerSig accounting
  command: grep -q 'missingAll' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q "emit('judge_skipped'" tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'implementation does not exist yet; write the artifact first' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF '!last.ok && !last.mech' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'existsSync, readFileSync } from "fs"' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal loop keeps a per-criterion measured/expected ledger from judge NACKs and injects a PARAMETER HISTORY table into the worker checkpoint when >=2 different measured values exist for the same criterion (capped at 5 entries)
  command: grep -q 'PARAMETER HISTORY' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'harvest' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'withHist' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'e.length > 5' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'interpolate/bisect' tools/goal.mjs
- label: goal loop single-blocker fast lane: when a real (non-mech) judge NACK has exactly one failing criterion (canonical [FAIL] lines or markdown FAIL rows) and remaining budget is under 30% of total, the next worker gets a surgical brief (single criterion verbatim + parameter history, fix-only-this directive) with strategy/exploration scaffolding dropped, preempting blind salvage
  command: grep -q 'SINGLE-BLOCKER FAST LANE' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'failLines' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q 'fastLane' tools/goal.mjs && grep -q "budget() / totalS < 0.3" tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal planner mandates an AMBIGUITIES section resolving every interpretation fork as a DECISION line with verbatim quoted evidence ([DERIVED]) or an [ASSUMED — verify both branches] tag; DECISION lines are parsed from the plan and echoed verbatim as a DECISIONS block into every worker prompt, the fast-lane surgical brief, and the salvage brief
  command: grep -qF 'AMBIGUITIES' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'DECISION: <fork> → <choice> BECAUSE' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'ASSUMED — verify both branches' tools/goal.mjs && test "$(grep -c 'decBlock}' tools/goal.mjs)" -ge 3 && grep -qF 'DECISIONS (interpretation forks already resolved' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal loop strategy-ladder pivot: planner emits STRATEGY_LADDER (primary/fallback/switch trigger); past 30% budget with declared artifacts still missing and no live jobs, a one-shot PIVOT MANDATE quoting the fallback verbatim prefixes the next worker prompt and emits a pivot event — it replaces that iteration's 40% draft-gate escalation (escalation stays available later), is mech-NACK/blockerSig exempt, and workers are told judge feedback WINS over contradicted DECISION lines
  command: grep -qF 'STRATEGY_LADDER' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'PIVOT MANDATE: >30% budget spent with no artifact' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF "emit('pivot'" tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF '(totalS - budget()) / totalS > 0.3' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF '!fastLane && !piv && !escalated' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF '!last.mech && !esc && !piv' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'judge feedback WINS' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
- label: goal planner is discovery-first with a provisional guard: the very first output is a minimal provisional ARTIFACTS line plus a one-line AMBIGUITIES (so a planner timeout still leaves a parseable plan), then discovery runs, then the FULL section block (ARTIFACTS, AMBIGUITIES, STRATEGY_LADDER with structurally-different fallback and switch-class-after-two-same-criterion-failures mandate, VERIFIER_SHAPE_CONTRACT, ...) is derived from discovered evidence; ARTIFACTS parsing is lenient (last inline ARTIFACTS: line wins, markdown/bare header form with paths on following lines accepted, 'none' → no artifacts) and DECISION lines are parsed from anywhere in a line, verbatim from DECISION: onward
  command: grep -qF 'PROVISIONAL GUARD — VERY FIRST output' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'DISCOVERY NEXT — evidence before contract' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'THEN emit the FULL section block' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'STRUCTURALLY different tool/algorithm/approach CLASS' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'starting hypothesis, not a commitment' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'matchAll(/ARTIFACTS:' tools/goal.mjs && grep -qF 'DECISION:.*$' tools/goal.mjs
  tags: [implemented]

# observability
- label: SSE parser prints '[provider] Name (model)' to stderr once per distinct provider value per process when chunks carry a top-level provider field (OpenRouter); no-op when absent
  command: grep -q 'seenProviders' index.mjs && grep -q '\[provider\]' index.mjs
  tags: [implemented]
